<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Dr. King comes for a preventive visit between his depression reviews. He has taken sertraline for three weeks, at 50 mg for two, with mild nausea for a few days that has passed. He has had three therapy sessions and has kept a fixed rising time; he is sleeping a little better. He has kept one day a week free of work twice in three weeks. He has no thoughts of harming himself. He still smokes about a pack a day, mostly late at night while writing, and now wants to set a quit date and use a medicine. His home blood pressure readings are being collected this week. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 36</td></tr><tr><td>Sertraline</td><td>Three weeks, 50 mg for two; early nausea passed</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-9 13; no thoughts of self-harm</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>About 20 cigarettes a day; ready to quit</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient on paper in a private room and reviewed with him face to face by Dr. Ashby-Nwankwo. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Fair; tired</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Low mood, improving; sustained threats; supportive family, church and colleagues</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>About a pack a day for over ten years; ready to quit</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>Occasional; AUDIT-C 2</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Little; long hours in cars and on platforms</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Irregular meals on the road; much fried and salted food</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Five to six hours; improving</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>Married; no concerns raised</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>Personal security arranged by his organization; wears a seat belt</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Normal by his report</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

