<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan made. Tdap given. Lipids and hemoglobin A1c were checked at intake. HIV, hepatitis C and hepatitis B screening ordered. Colorectal screening due at 45. [S]<list><item>Hepatitis B vaccination to start once the screening result is back.</item><item>Influenza vaccine in the autumn.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Nicotine dependence, cigarettes (F17.210)</content>. Ready to quit. After discussing nicotine replacement, varenicline and bupropion, he chose varenicline, the most effective single medicine; the EAGLES trial found no significant rise in serious neuropsychiatric events in smokers with psychiatric disorders, and his mood will be watched. Starting it three weeks after sertraline lets side effects be told apart. [S]<list><item>Varenicline 0.5 mg daily for three days, then twice daily for four days, then 1 mg twice daily, after food.</item><item>Quit date one week from today.</item><item>Weekly telephone counseling with the quitline and a written plan for late-night writing without cigarettes.</item><item>Report any worsening of mood, agitation or unusual thoughts at once.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder, single episode, moderate (F32.1)</content>. PHQ-9 13, from 17, three weeks into treatment; no suicidal ideation. [S]<list><item>Safety plan reviewed and unchanged; 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline and the clinic number confirmed.</item><item>Continue sertraline 50 mg, therapy and CBT for insomnia.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>134/86 mmHg; home readings this week to confirm</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 13 on treatment; followed in his depression care</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Counseled for about 10 minutes; varenicline started; quit date set</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use</td><td>Up to date</td><td>AUDIT-C 2 at intake; no change</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol and cardiovascular risk</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Lipids at intake: LDL 142 mg/dL; lifestyle; recheck in about four months</td></tr><tr><td>Prediabetes and diabetes screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Overweight, age 35 to 70: hemoglobin A1c 5.5 percent at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not yet due; starts at 45</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time screening for adults 15 to 65; drawn today with his agreement</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time antibody test for adults 18 to 79; drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time triple panel drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tdap today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended for adults 19 to 59; to start once the screening result is known</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>In the autumn</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Tdap vaccine [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Tobacco Smoking Cessation in Adults, Including Pregnant Persons: Interventions (2021); Neuropsychiatric safety and efficacy of varenicline, bupropion, and nicotine patch in smokers with and without psychiatric disorders (EAGLES) (2016); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Quit date in one week; quitline call in one week. Eight-week review in three weeks with home blood pressure readings. Next scheduled visit 1965-06-02: eight-week review: mood, sleep, sertraline, smoking cessation and home blood pressure. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
